{"skill":{"slug":"initiation-of-coverage-or-deep-dive","displayName":"Initiation of Coverage Agent"},"version":{"version":"1.0.4","createdAt":1776424717457,"changelog":"Publish 1.0.4","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":7152,"sha256":"6d3554d62a3da2b5ba00ff1eb728e39d400f2ffe6f828d98c51854dc75c5cf8d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/generate_deep_research_report.py","size":10015,"sha256":"8d270701d4917f53108e4bd71ccfba55a4c6998656b9cce5620b5b94281f8693","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2699,"sha256":"6df05933e5feec352c84b8d2872b94afd510c6b52189d6385bb3a3cd94cde726","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789438441613,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"15561130c8c4572cb35331ee39bc17410065b6115cad9720d7e4eeaedf8e90de","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/15561130c8c4572cb35331ee39bc17410065b6115cad9720d7e4eeaedf8e90de","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780086698005},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":28,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789438441613},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill appears purpose-built for generating stock research reports, but it uses an API key and sends the user's original query to an external service with some under-scoped and unsafe credential-handling details users should review.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access, the EM_API_KEY environment variable, and report file writes are purpose-aligned, but the artifact does not define a tight allowed-tools or permission boundary and the script allows caller-controlled output directories.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill declares the required EM_API_KEY and installs httpx, but the dependency is unpinned, making installation less reproducible and more exposed to upstream package changes.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The trigger scope includes generic requests for a company research report, and the skill forwards the original user query to the backend API without a clear confirmation or user-facing privacy notice for ambiguous requests.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No persistence, background worker, scheduled task, or privilege escalation was found, but the script follows redirects while sending a custom API-key header, creating an avoidable credential-disclosure risk if the fixed API endpoint redirects unexpectedly.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose, script behavior, Eastmoney API use, and local PDF/DOCX attachment output are coherent for generating first-coverage or deep-dive company reports.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this skill before installing. It will use an EM_API_KEY, send your original prompt to Eastmoney's report-generation API, and save generated report files locally. Avoid using it for prompts containing confidential information, and prefer a version that disables unsafe redirects, pins dependencies, and clearly scopes network, environment-variable, and file-write permissions.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The API key, network call, and attachment writes fit the report-generation purpose, but the lack of explicit scope remains a real review concern rather than evidence of malicious behavior.\n[SQP-1] expected: Triggering for company research-report requests is aligned with the skill, but the broad trigger can cause external API calls when the user did not clearly intend this specific workflow.\n[SQP-2] expected: Passing the original query to the external report service is functionally necessary here, but the artifact does not give a clear user-facing disclosure or confirmation step.\n[T09] unexpected: The artifact-backed follow_redirects=True behavior with a custom em_api_key header is not needed for the stated purpose and creates a concrete credential-handling weakness.\n[T08] expected: Using httpx is expected for the API integration, but installing it without a pinned version or hash is a supply-chain hygiene issue.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789438441613}}}}}